{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>Come up to Me to the mountain.</b> This passage too was said before the giving of the Torah, and the wording proves as much: 'and I will give you the tablets of stone, and the Torah and the commandment.' <b>And be there.</b> Rashi, of blessed memory, explained: forty days." "<b>Which I have written.</b> That is, before the world was created, for the Torah was written before Him in black fire upon white fire. Or, 'which I have written' refers back to the tablets of stone that He mentioned, which were written by the finger of Elohim." "<b>To instruct them.</b> By way of the plain sense (peshat): this teaches you that the Torah and the commandments are a paved road and a path for the soul to return to its root, and this is the sense of להורותם — that is, to instruct them in the way to the World to Come. Thus Solomon, peace be upon him, said (Proverbs 4:4): ״ויורני ויאמר לי יתמך דבריך לבך שמור מצותי וחיה״." "<b>And by way of the Midrash:</b> להורותם — 'to instruct them' — this is Talmud. And so they expounded in tractate Berakhot: את לחות האבן — 'the tablets of stone,' these are the tablets; והתורה — 'and the Torah,' this is the written Torah; והמצוה — 'and the commandment,' this is the Mishnah; אשר כתבתי — 'which I have written,' these are the Prophets and Writings; להורותם — 'to instruct them,' this is Talmud — teaching that all of them were given to Moses from Sinai. And furthermore, you will find in להורותם: the letter lamed and the letter mem spell ל״ם, seventy, with 'Torah' in the middle, and this alludes to the seventy faces of the Torah." "<b>And by way of the Kabbalah:</b> להורותם is written, and it is a proof to what was explained, that the Torah and the commandment guide a person toward this attribute, which is Knesset Yisrael, and from there the soul ascends to the World to Come, in the manner of the verse (Psalms 73:24): ״ואחר כבוד תקחני״ — 'and afterward, glory, You will take me' — 'You'; and understand this. And the sense of להורותם is like (Song of Songs 3:4): ״ואל חדר הורתי״ — 'and into the chamber of her who conceived me.'"], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:03:42.125614315Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}